id: pm-15yuly
title: Keep the largest list prefix that fits the output budget
description: Increasing the requested list limit can return fewer rows because the reported compaction strategy halves the candidate size.
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-09-18T03:55:15.799Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-18T09:45:07.901Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-18T09:45:07.269Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-18T09:45:07.269Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: "Choose the largest prefix fitting the complete rendered partial-response envelope; increasing requests within the truncated-envelope regime must not exhibit halving oscillation. Keep applied limits, cursor offsets, nested row declarations, and session charges consistent. Document the unavoidable metadata-cost difference at the complete-to-partial boundary."
parent: pm-5t33or
severity: medium
repro_steps: "Create 130 items; compare list limits 20, 30, 40, 50, 60, 80, 100 and 130 with output budget 1500. Reporter observed 20, 15, 20, 12, 15, 20, 12 and 16 rows respectively."
resolution: Replaced lossy halving with largest-fitting-prefix search over the complete rendered envelope; preserved hidden nested row declarations and consistent pre-selection session charges.
expected_result: "Maximal useful prefixes within the emitted partial-response budget, accurate applied limits and resumable cursor offsets, with the complete-to-partial metadata boundary documented."
actual_result: 8997 tests pass; 100/100/100/100 exact coverage; 300 boundary cases have zero overruns; manual list requests 20 through 130 consistently retain 12 rows under 1500 tokens; contracts discovery retains 77 rather than 68 summaries under 4500 tokens.
affected_version: 2026.9.17
component: SDK read-output budgets
