comments[9]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-18T03:55:15.799Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: searched all statuses for the issue numbers and precise largest-prefix and receipt-overhead wording; inspected the canonical output-budget parent and closed read fallback lineage; inspected current open and in-progress inventories. No existing focused item owns this newly reported behavior. Keep this intake open and unclaimed until implementation starts."
  "2026-09-18T08:29:34.649Z","harness:codex","rendered-prefix regression failed before implementation, reproducing halving waste. Candidate prefixes now include full continuation, producer cursor, count/applied_limit, session and UTF-8 renderer costs before selection. A complete response and a truncated response have different mandatory envelope costs; unconditional monotonicity across that boundary conflicts with no-op receipt elision. The guarantee is maximal fitting prefix for the emitted truncated envelope, not equal metadata costs across complete and partial results."
  "2026-09-18T08:37:16.686Z","harness:codex","Manual rendered-output inspection exposed additional avoidable headroom: internal row-contract metadata was counted before the transport removed it. The SDK now retains row declarations internally during compaction and session accounting but excludes them from emitted-byte measurement unless explicitly requested. Added nested object-map and session regressions, including one-more-row infeasibility and cursor offsets. Final full coverage must run after this correction."
  "2026-09-18T08:46:53.135Z","harness:codex","Strict static verification caught a complexity overflow and context-session calibration drift. Extracted largest reducible collection selection without relaxing complexity limits. Preserved legacy top-level session accounting alongside hidden nested selectors; the unchanged two-item/2243-item calibration now passes, including complete cursor walks and prior spend/seen-item ceilings. Added a mixed nested graph plus activity regression. Final coverage remains pending."
  "2026-09-18T08:57:11.669Z","harness:codex","Differential SDK experiment against the unchanged main implementation on identical contract-summary input: old halving retained 68 command summaries; new maximal fitting prefix retains 77. The agent-task token baseline increase (4108 to 4458 in its canonical fixture) is additional delivered content, not a new receipt. Recalibrating the generated measurement artifact is appropriate for the requested largest-prefix behavior; the 4500-token default ceiling and negative-control enforcement remain unchanged. An independently discovered full-contracts no-op receipt was also removed and covered by regression."
  "2026-09-18T09:02:13.964Z","harness:codex",A finite boundary sweep of mixed nested graph and top-level activity rows reproduced 95 rendered-envelope overruns across budgets 1000 through 3990 before correction. Session accounting now enumerates declared nested rows plus undeclared top-level arrays consistently before and after prefix selection. Added 1000/1010/1600-token regressions with and without sessions. Interrupted the in-flight coverage run because these source changes require a new stable-source run; the interrupted run is not proof.
  "2026-09-18T09:09:51.809Z","harness:codex","Stable-source verification: the mixed nested/activity boundary sweep now passes all 300 budgets with zero rendered overruns; the prior implementation failed 95. Strict local complexity and 100 percent module/export/member docstring gates pass. SDK import-cost and CLI transport floors pass. All ten graph-composition assertions plus record-integrity pass after linking cited evidence. Full coverage is running and has not yet completed."
  "2026-09-18T09:31:41.814Z","harness:codex","Full stable-source run: all 705 files and 8996 tests passed. Exact coverage was statements 64808/64808, functions 13451/13451, lines 62029/62029, branches 49453/49455. Two uncovered branches prevented acceptance: added a real object-map no-op versus binding-limit regression, and removed a now-redundant applied_limit guard in cursor rebasing because the prefix selector already assigns that value for every retained items candidate. No ignore directive, threshold relaxation, or mocked coverage workaround was introduced. Final exact coverage rerun required."
  "2026-09-18T09:45:06.459Z","harness:codex","Final verification passed on stable sources: 705 test files, 8997 tests; exact coverage statements 64806/64806, branches 49453/49453, functions 13451/13451, lines 62027/62027. Runner: node scripts/run-tests.mjs coverage -- --maxWorkers=4 --coverage.reportOnFailure. All coverage thresholds remain 100 with zero uncovered counts. Packed npm/npx/Bun/bunx, real 131-item Node/Bun acceptance, 300 mixed-session boundary cases, static complexity/docstrings, unchanged context calibration, SDK/CLI performance floors, graph and record-integrity assertions passed. Prepared for reviewed delivery; hosted exact-head checks remain a separate requirement."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-18T09:32:57.594Z","harness:codex","Measure the final envelope at every candidate prefix: continuation offsets, applied limits, visible schema metadata and session identities can change the cost. Keep structural row declarations internally even when omitted from transport. Verify one-more-row infeasibility and mixed nested/top-level session facts near the binding ceiling; row-halving and post-selection metadata patches can both waste or exceed the budget."
